<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  HomesteadDefenseLeague.xml              Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  Builds FACTION_SPEC.md section 3, "Homestead Defense League ; PATCH vanilla
  `OutlanderCivil`". A reskin, not a new def.

  READ FROM THE SHIPPED DEF, 2026-08-14 ; not inferred:
  C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\RimWorld\Data\Core\Defs\
    FactionDefs\Factions_Misc.xml

      ParentName                  OutlanderFactionBase
      OWN nodes                   defName · label · description · colorSpectrum ·
                                  classicIdeo · maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation ·
                                  configurationListOrderPriority
      label                       civil outlander union

  🔴 EVERYTHING ELSE IS ON THE ABSTRACT PARENT, NOT ON THIS DEF.
  `OutlanderFactionBase` is where `pawnSingular`, `pawnsPlural`, `leaderTitle`
  and `settlementGenerationWeight` actually live. PatchOperations run BEFORE
  def inheritance is resolved, so at patch time `OutlanderCivil` literally does
  not have those nodes. A `Replace` on any of them matches ZERO and logs red.
  They are `Add`s onto the child, and the child's own node wins at inheritance
  time, which is exactly the override we want and reaches `OutlanderCivil`
  ALONE ; patching the parent would also hit OutlanderRough and every modded
  descendant.

      pawnSingular / pawnsPlural  parent      ->  Add
      leaderTitle                 parent      ->  Add
      settlementGenerationWeight  parent (1)  ->  Add
      raidsForbidden              ABSENT in the whole chain  ->  Add
      label / description         own nodes   ->  Replace

  ⛔ `pawnGroupMakers`, `factionNameMaker` and the raid curves are untouched.
  They are inherited and already balanced; R15's group surgery is the Empire's
  alone.

  ⚠️ `raidsForbidden` is the MECHANISM for R2, not a precept. It is what makes
  the League never raid the player, and it has no vanilla default here.

  ⚠️ The ideo layer (`fixedIdeo` / `ideoName` "the Covenant of Free Wells" /
  `deityPresets`) is NOT in this file. It lands in `FactionReligions.xml` in
  its own pass, the same way the Empire's did.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Everything sits inside a conditional on the def existing, so the file is a
  silent no-op rather than a wall of red if the vessel ever moves. Every
  defName written here is vanilla Core, so no `MayRequire` is owed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- "civil outlander union" -> the campaign name. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]/label</xpath>
          <value><label>Homestead Defense League</label></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]/description</xpath>
          <value>
            <description>The most numerous and least centralised faction on the world — farmers on the dry flats, living off whatever their vaporators pull out of the night air.\n\nDecent, tired, and badly armed. They defend wells and they do not come looking for anyone.</description>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- Inherited from OutlanderFactionBase. Add, not Replace. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnSingular>moisture farmer</pawnSingular></value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><pawnsPlural>moisture farmers</pawnsPlural></value>
        </li>

        <!-- "prime councilor" on the parent -> High Marshal. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><leaderTitle>High Marshal</leaderTitle></value>
        </li>

        <!-- R2's mechanism. Absent throughout the chain, so this creates it. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><raidsForbidden>true</raidsForbidden></value>
        </li>

        <!-- 1 on the parent -> 1.9. Thirteen settlements, the most on the map. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value><settlementGenerationWeight>1.9</settlementGenerationWeight></value>
        </li>

        <!--
          ================================================================
          faction_religions_spec.md entry 3 (B54)
          ================================================================
          `ideoName` and `ideoDescription` verbatim; they are the only strings
          the engine renders. ⛔ `hiddenIdeo` MUST STAY UNSET or the
          description is never shown. Structure meme goes FIRST in
          `forcedMemes`.

          `OutlanderCivil` ships `classicIdeo true`. It is removed: an authored
          `fixedIdeo` is not the classic single-ideo mode, and vanilla's only
          `fixedIdeo` def (HoraxCult) carries neither that nor `disallowedMemes`.
        -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]/classicIdeo</xpath>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="OutlanderCivil"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
            <requiredPreceptsOnly>false</requiredPreceptsOnly>
            <ideoName>the Covenant of Free Wells</ideoName>
            <ideoDescription>Water was given once and the Giver stepped back, and we have not been spoken to since. That is not abandonment. It is the test. A well belongs to whoever is thirsty standing at it — we have never turned a stranger away, and we have buried our own for it. We do not take up arms and go out. We stand on our own ground, we keep the vaporators turning, and we answer to the silence.</ideoDescription>
            <forcedMemes>
              <li>Structure_TheistAbstract</li>
              <li MayRequire="sarg.alphamemes">AM_WaterPrimacy</li>
              <li>Individualist</li>
              <li>Guilty</li>
              <li>Rancher</li>
            </forcedMemes>
            <deityPresets>
              <li>
                <nameType><name>the Withdrawn</name><type>That Which Was Given</type></nameType>
                <gender>None</gender>
                <iconPath>UI/Deities/DeityGeneric</iconPath>
              </li>
            </deityPresets>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
